---
/**
 * About page — explains the product using the project's own framing.
 * Facts are sourced from README.md / CLAUDE.md (corridor model, source-verified
 * claims, two-reviewer rule, build gate, "informational only"). No invented claims.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Relocation Guide"
  description="Relocation Guide gives source-backed, independently verified relocation guidance organised by origin and destination country."
>
  <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-2xl space-y-8">
    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">About Relocation Guide</h1>
      <p class="text-slate-600">
        Moving to another country means making legal, financial, and life-altering
        decisions from scattered, fast-changing information. Relocation Guide brings the
        steps for your specific move into one place &mdash; and shows you exactly where
        each fact comes from.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Guidance by corridor</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700">
        Our content is organised by <strong>corridor</strong> &mdash; your origin country
        paired with your destination country &mdash; because the rules that apply to you
        depend on both. You tell the planner where you are moving from and to, why you are
        moving, and a few details about your situation; it then shows the steps that apply
        to <em>you</em>, in order, with the documents you will need for each one.
      </p>
      <p class="text-slate-700">
        Our first corridor is <strong>USA &rarr; Switzerland</strong>, covering the work,
        family-reunification, retirement, and study routes. More corridors are in
        preparation and will appear once they pass the same checks.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">How we keep it accurate</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700">
        Accuracy is the whole point, so we built the site around it:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-slate-700">
        <li>
          <strong>Every claim has an official source.</strong> Each fact is traced to a
          primary, official authority &mdash; not a blog or a forum.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Two independent checks.</strong> The person who writes a claim and the
          person who verifies it are never the same. A claim is only published after a
          separate reviewer confirms it against the source.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Dated and shown to you.</strong> Each page displays its sources and the
          date the facts were last verified, so you can judge how current they are.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Stale facts can't slip through.</strong> Our publishing process refuses
          to release a page if any claim on it is unverified or overdue for re-checking.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Your answers stay with you</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700">
        The planner runs in your browser. The answers you give are saved on your own
        device, not on our servers, and there are no accounts to create. You can clear
        everything at any time. See our <a href="/privacy">Privacy policy</a> for details.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">What we are not</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700">
        Relocation Guide is <strong>information, not advice</strong>. We are not a law firm
        and not licensed immigration advisers, and using the site does not create an
        advisory relationship. Immigration rules change often, so always confirm your
        situation with the official authority or a licensed adviser before acting.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Get in touch</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700">
        Spotted something out of date, or have a question? See our
        <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>. Operator details are in our
        <a href="/impressum">Impressum</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
